WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.165
An OSINT workstation is a controlled environment for legitimate, organized,

00:00:04.165 --> 00:00:06.042
and repeatable public-source research.

00:00:06.042 --> 00:00:10.400
Separation from personal browsing reduces contamination and supports clear handling of

00:00:10.400 --> 00:00:10.760
settings,

00:00:10.760 --> 00:00:12.800
accounts, case files, and evidence.

00:00:12.800 --> 00:00:16.840
Design starts with investigation types, privacy rules, storage, browser workflows,

00:00:16.840 --> 00:00:19.870
documentation, auditability, and recovery.

00:00:19.870 --> 00:00:23.380
Hardware and operating systems should be supported, reliable, and maintainable.

00:00:23.380 --> 00:00:25.970
Complexity is useful only when it solves a defined risk.

00:00:25.970 --> 00:00:29.705
Dedicated browser profiles, structured notes, source logs, timestamps,

00:00:29.705 --> 00:00:34.160
contextual captures, and raw-versus-analysis separation preserve traceability.

00:00:34.160 --> 00:00:37.485
Security depends on updates, strong authentication, endpoint protection,

00:00:37.485 --> 00:00:40.200
account separation, access limits, and ethical boundaries.

00:00:40.200 --> 00:00:43.800
Encrypted storage, tested backups, retention schedules, cleanup,

00:00:43.800 --> 00:00:46.840
and audit trails protect case material throughout its lifecycle.

00:00:46.840 --> 00:00:50.060
Tools should be selected for workflow value, security, data handling,

00:00:50.060 --> 00:00:52.955
and export quality rather than popularity or novelty.

00:00:52.955 --> 00:00:54.750
The goal is disciplined intelligence work,

00:00:54.750 --> 00:00:57.525
not collecting tools or claiming perfect anonymity.

00:00:57.525 --> 00:01:01.010
A good workstation helps analysts answer scoped questions, validate evidence,

00:01:01.010 --> 00:01:03.600
document reasoning, protect sensitive information,

00:01:03.600 --> 00:01:06.480
and report responsibly under organizational policy and law.
